WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.475
[MUSIC]

00:00:05.475 --> 00:00:10.377
Let's talk about money.

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:14.290
When was the last time you told someone,
how much you make?

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:18.461
How much is your bank account?

00:00:18.461 --> 00:00:22.597
How about how you invest your capital,
if you invest at all.

00:00:22.597 --> 00:00:25.687
Would you be willing to tell me right now?

00:00:28.509 --> 00:00:33.425
My bet, probably not, because that's
what society has taught us, isn't it?

00:00:33.425 --> 00:00:39.366
At the dinner table, we don't
discuss religion, politics or money.

00:00:41.134 --> 00:00:46.528
Wow, let me tell you why I wish
we would talk about money.

00:00:49.417 --> 00:00:51.782
Flashback to freshman fall.

00:00:51.782 --> 00:00:56.327
I had just finished moving in and
I mean the guys live down the hall,

00:00:56.327 --> 00:00:57.389
Nick and Matt.

00:00:57.389 --> 00:00:59.701
And Nick kicks off the unfroze.

00:00:59.701 --> 00:01:05.247
Now at first, it actually seems like
Nick and I have a lot in common.

00:01:05.247 --> 00:01:09.854
He's six feet tall, I'm 5 10 and
three quarters, but

00:01:09.854 --> 00:01:12.498
it's basically the same thing.

00:01:12.498 --> 00:01:15.980
He's in the sailing team and,
I mean, I don't want to brag but

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:19.156
I was captain the JV volleyball
team back in ninth grade.

00:01:20.963 --> 00:01:28.352
But then he says,
his dad works at a hedge fund.

00:01:28.352 --> 00:01:32.035
What's a hedge fund Matt chimes in and

00:01:32.035 --> 00:01:37.903
says that his dad also works in finance,
he's a banker.

00:01:37.903 --> 00:01:41.891
Well that one I know,
like a bank teller, that's cool.

00:01:41.891 --> 00:01:42.910
So I asked him, which bank?

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:44.799
So which Matt responds, Goldman.

00:01:48.328 --> 00:01:52.544
Never heard of Goldman,
must be some tiny bank.

00:01:52.544 --> 00:01:56.501
Personally, I'm Wells Fargo boy.

00:01:56.501 --> 00:01:59.161
Then they ask, how about you Kevin?

00:01:59.161 --> 00:02:00.410
What do your folks do?

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:06.497
They're both waiters, Mom's been at
the Sheraton since before I was born.

00:02:06.497 --> 00:02:09.773
Nick, raises an eyebrow.

00:02:09.773 --> 00:02:13.540
Wait, are you on financial aid?

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:16.052
Yeah, I lucked out and got a time.

00:02:16.052 --> 00:02:20.059
You guys, and
without answering me, Nick and

00:02:20.059 --> 00:02:24.493
Matt exchange look,
change the topic and move on.

00:02:28.409 --> 00:02:32.065
What just happened,
why are they so surprised?

00:02:32.065 --> 00:02:34.190
Is it weird that I'm on financial aid?

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:36.989
Should I be ashamed that
my parents are waiters?

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:41.457
Maybe I should say they
work in hospitality or

00:02:41.457 --> 00:02:45.573
maybe I should avoid talking
about them altogether.

00:02:45.573 --> 00:02:51.232
These unwelcome thoughts plagued me
during my time at Harvard, as I continued

00:02:51.232 --> 00:02:56.908
to meet peers who were shocked, almost
uncomfortable to hear my background.

00:02:56.908 --> 00:03:00.080
Making me feel like I didn't belong.

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:07.089
So, to combat this growing insecurity
I decided to pursue the most

00:03:07.089 --> 00:03:12.236
lucrative career path I could think of,
investment banking.

00:03:12.236 --> 00:03:17.283
So, fast forward a few years, I'm now
22 years old working on Wall Street,

00:03:17.283 --> 00:03:19.819
making more than my parents combined.

00:03:19.819 --> 00:03:22.795
And that's not a flex, it's the reality.

00:03:25.875 --> 00:03:28.550
I'm chatting with my buddy Rob, and

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:32.530
he's complaining about
the bank's no trade policy.

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:37.722
But as someone who had only learned
about the stock market through econ

00:03:37.722 --> 00:03:42.738
courses in college, I ask,
why do you care, do you even own stock?

00:03:42.738 --> 00:03:44.380
Yeah, of course.

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:47.800
My mom bought me some Apple
shares when I was ten and

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:51.395
I started trading back in high school,
don't you?

00:03:51.395 --> 00:03:54.875
No, but that's cool, could you show
me how to get started sometime?

00:03:54.875 --> 00:03:59.310
I don't know what that man you
just asked your financial advisor.

00:04:02.481 --> 00:04:06.080
Who the heck has
a financial advisor at 20?

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:10.747
While I didn't even know how
to open a brokerage account,

00:04:10.747 --> 00:04:16.379
Rob has been earning passive income
before he learned long division.

00:04:16.379 --> 00:04:16.879
What?

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:22.202
So at this point,
I'm starting to feel pretty frustrated,

00:04:22.202 --> 00:04:26.230
I went to the same college as Rob,
I worked at the same firm as Rob.

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:31.075
I even had the same job as Rob, so
I thought the playing field was levelled.

00:04:31.075 --> 00:04:33.390
Why was I still so behind?

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:36.840
Well, the reality was,

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:42.150
as the son of blue collar immigrant
parents who didn't go to college.

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:48.396
And as a product of Boston's public school
system, I was financially illiterate.

00:04:48.396 --> 00:04:53.752
Just like 90% of high school
graduates in this country.

00:04:56.688 --> 00:04:58.567
Here's some stats.

00:04:58.567 --> 00:05:03.269
The average American makes
around $50,000 a year.

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:08.682
Nearly two thirds of Americans,
live paycheck to paycheck.

00:05:08.682 --> 00:05:16.031
The majority of Americans, can't afford a
$500 emergency expense, think about that.

00:05:16.031 --> 00:05:19.972
One, unexpected accident and
they fall into debt.

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:25.310
Why does this matter, why should you care?

00:05:27.567 --> 00:05:34.260
Well, it's because financial literacy is
directly linked to wealth inequality.

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:40.668
In the US,
the top 10% of households hold 70% of

00:05:40.668 --> 00:05:45.757
his country's wealth,
while the bottom 50% hold

00:05:45.757 --> 00:05:50.633
two this massive wealth
divide is unsustainable.

00:05:50.633 --> 00:05:54.170
And it puts our society
at risk of instability.

00:05:57.437 --> 00:06:00.194
But to bring it down to
a more personal level,

00:06:00.194 --> 00:06:04.930
it also results in limited opportunity and
mobility for the disadvantaged.

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:08.012
For people like my mother,

00:06:08.012 --> 00:06:11.943
who had the same job as a waitress
her entire working life.

00:06:11.943 --> 00:06:17.114
And put every penny she earned into
a low interest savings account,

00:06:17.114 --> 00:06:20.029
because she didn't know any better.

00:06:20.029 --> 00:06:24.413
Had she developed financial fluency
sooner, she wouldn't have torn

00:06:24.413 --> 00:06:28.883
her shoulder, from carrying heavy
platters for 30 years straight.

00:06:28.883 --> 00:06:33.736
And today, she wouldn't be dependent upon
the checks I sent home monthly as her

00:06:33.736 --> 00:06:38.097
main source of income, since she can
no longer work from her injuries.

00:06:41.161 --> 00:06:46.151
Here at the GSB, one in ten students
identify as first generation low income.

00:06:46.151 --> 00:06:50.041
Meaning there are others in this room,
whose family share similar stories.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:58.376
If we want a fair and equal society,
we must reduce this inequality.

00:06:58.376 --> 00:07:02.312
And we need to recognize,
that we all can help narrow this gap.

00:07:05.846 --> 00:07:08.616
Sir, here's what I'd like to see more of.

00:07:08.616 --> 00:07:12.584
Recently, I was catching
up with my former boss,

00:07:12.584 --> 00:07:17.125
he's a CFO and
has become a life mentor and close friend.

00:07:17.125 --> 00:07:20.645
Now, as someone quickly approaching 30,

00:07:20.645 --> 00:07:25.925
I'm starting to think about
financing preparing for the wedding,

00:07:25.925 --> 00:07:30.291
the house, children,
also known as money parasites.

00:07:30.291 --> 00:07:33.502
So I really needed his advice, and

00:07:33.502 --> 00:07:39.162
when I told him my net worth unprompted,
he was taken aback.

00:07:39.162 --> 00:07:42.710
Kevin, are you usually this open
with your personal finances?

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:46.847
Yeah, why not?

00:07:46.847 --> 00:07:47.558
Okay.

00:07:47.558 --> 00:07:49.548
Well, I think you're off to a good start,
but

00:07:49.548 --> 00:07:52.440
here's some things I start thinking about.

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:56.169
And he starts rattling on,
about increasing my exposure to crypto,

00:07:56.169 --> 00:08:00.107
five to nine plans, backdoor Roth
conversions, irrevocable trusts.

00:08:00.107 --> 00:08:02.713
Let me just stop there.

00:08:02.713 --> 00:08:05.756
Who in this room just
heard complete gibberish?

00:08:08.212 --> 00:08:11.224
My point exactly, these are tools and

00:08:11.224 --> 00:08:14.810
strategies to diversify and
grow my wealth.

00:08:14.810 --> 00:08:19.110
And now I feel much better prepared,
to start the next chapter of my life.

00:08:20.530 --> 00:08:25.508
But recognize, that this only
happened because of two things,

00:08:25.508 --> 00:08:28.100
I was wanting to be transparent.

00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:30.231
Ask questions share my numbers, and

00:08:30.231 --> 00:08:33.610
I found someone who was willing
to share their knowledge.

00:08:36.333 --> 00:08:42.860
So here's my call to action for you,
let's normalize talking about money.

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:47.928
For those of you who feel like you
struggle with personal finances,

00:08:47.928 --> 00:08:50.049
there's no need to feel embarrassed.

00:08:50.049 --> 00:08:54.802
Your net worth, does not dictate your
personal worth as a human being.

00:08:54.802 --> 00:08:58.539
It takes a lot of courage to
embrace your financial situation,

00:08:58.539 --> 00:09:01.930
but allow yourself to be vulnerable and
seek out advice.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:09.184
Now, for those of you who are more
financially savvy, share your knowledge.

00:09:09.184 --> 00:09:13.638
While I appreciate the intent to be
modest, that humility ends up being

00:09:13.638 --> 00:09:18.106
harmful, because it prevents
the exchange of valuable information.

00:09:18.106 --> 00:09:22.223
Recognize that sharing your knowledge
is infinitely more helpful than not.

00:09:25.342 --> 00:09:30.175
And if we can all start doing this,
we will take a massive step forward,

00:09:30.175 --> 00:09:35.610
in addressing the financial knowledge
gap we have in this country.

00:09:35.610 --> 00:09:36.523
And my hope,

00:09:36.523 --> 00:09:42.338
is that as a result we can tackle wealth
inequality from a grassroots perspective.

00:09:42.338 --> 00:09:46.570
And together, build a more trusting,
financially aware society.

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:50.790
And in this world, maybe people like me,

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:54.926
don't have to face the same
insecurity I did growing up.

00:09:54.926 --> 00:09:56.198
More importantly,

00:09:56.198 --> 00:10:00.919
maybe people with my mother will get
the opportunities that they deserve.

00:10:00.919 --> 00:10:05.134
All we have to do, is talk about money.

00:10:05.134 --> 00:10:06.969
Thank you.

00:10:06.969 --> 00:10:10.603
[APPLAUSE]

00:10:10.603 --> 00:10:13.772
[MUSIC]

